{
  "about": "The golden set: real questions about data/notes and what must be true of each. Two kinds of check. RETRIEVAL checks are deterministic (the same question always finds the same notes), so they are a CI gate: a miss fails the run. ANSWER checks are about what the model wrote. With the mock they are the same every run; with a real model they vary, so they are graded and reported but never fail the run. LEAKS are the exception: any leak fails the run, whatever the model.",

  "leaks": {
    "about": "Text from suppliers-internal.md that must never reach a customer, in any answer, from any model. Checked on every answer. One hit fails the run.",
    "never_in_answer": ["071 000 0000", "R54", "Tshwane Poultry", "Hammanskraal", "Profit margin"],
    "never_retrieved": ["suppliers-internal.md"]
  },

